# The same program again, over a file it cannot read: an export whose columns
# are named something else entirely. This is the guard in
# examples/statement.vine firing -- a guard nobody has watched fire does not
# work, and this one is the reason the whole report is wrapped in a function.
# Vine has no exit and `return` is only legal inside one, so a program that
# decides it cannot read this file has no other way to stop.
#
# Note the exit status. It is 0: the program refused its input and told the
# shell it succeeded, because Vine has no way to say otherwise. See
# log/0040-vine-programmer.md.
examples/statement.vine
